+# Fifth and final pass: gaps, the Stenliden block and Lotsby — 2026-11-12
+
+This pass closes the Mariehamn street review. A survey of the city base after the fourth pass found too few datable streets left for another 10 km. Most undated streets are absent through 1995: Fågelberget, the Lotsby grid, Blomstringevägen and Skrapängsvägen. Others lie west of sheet 101208 (Möckelö), or are pieces of multi-carriageway junctions that need their own review. This pass dates what the maps support and records the rest.
+
+Newly dated: 3,034.94 m in 26 persistent objects (EPSG:3874), all new. Three objects are junction or lane pieces:
+
+- Nya Godbyvägen's junction with Bolstavägen: 13 pieces counted 0 m, because they are carriageways and turning lanes beside dated road.
+- Lotsgatan's two carriageways around an island: counted once, as the longer.
+- Uppgårdsvägen's link: counted once, as the longer lane.
+
+| First reviewed evidence | Newly dated metres |
+| --- | ---: |
+| 1968 | 896.21 |
+| 1978 (red overprint revision) | 0 (junction pieces only) |
+| 1985 | 970.46 |
+| 1995 | 1,168.27 |
+
+| Group | Metres | Streets and first evidence |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| Gaps in dated streets | 980.78 | 1968: two Sjukhusvägen gaps, Mariegatan, Skeppargatan's bend, Östra and Västra Esplanadgatan, two Sjöpromenaden pieces, Lotsgatan's island. 1985: Havsgatan's middle section, Neptunigatan's curve, two Hindersbölevägen pieces, Grindmattesvägen's link |
+| Stenliden | 1,208.02 | 1978: Nya Godbyvägen–Bolstavägen junction (0 m). 1985: Uppgårdsvägen's link. 1995: Uppgårdsvägen, Östra Stenliden, Kråkbärsstigen's eastern part, Blåbärsstigen (three parts), Hjortronstigen |
+| Lotsby and Ytternäs south | 846.14 | 1968: Fiskhamnsvägen (red road). 1985: Måsvägen, Doppingvägen |
+
+## Findings
+
+**The Stenliden block needed its junction.** The fourth pass deferred the block because it reached the dated network only through undated Nya Godbyvägen pieces. Those pieces lie between the second pass's north and south junctions (1978). They are drawn in the thick 1978 overprint together with the Bolstavägen approach, so they are dated from 1978 as one 0 m junction object. A short red link west from the junction is drawn in 1985 and becomes Uppgårdsvägen's entrance in 1995. With the junction and the link dated, Uppgårdsvägen and the streets off it start in 1995. Kråkbärsstigen's western part and Hjortronstigen's link connect today only through cycleways and stay deferred.
+
+**Gap pieces take their neighbours' edition only when the map shows them.** Sjukhusvägen's two gaps lie inside the 1968 road symbol, and Mariegatan's and the Esplanadgatans' pieces follow white streets between hatched blocks. All of these start in 1968. Havsgatan's middle section and Neptunigatan's curve run through hatched blocks in 1968. That evidence is *unclear*, and they start in 1985, when they are drawn as streets. Hamngatan's harbour pieces and Styrmansgatan are deferred, because the harbour area was rebuilt and their 1995 drawing is unclear.
+
+**Lotsby is later than 1995.** Skonertvägen, Briggstigen, Lotsbyvägen and the gränder around them appear in 1995 only as plan lines, and Segelmakargatan as a black line, so none is dated. Fiskhamnsvägen along the shore is a red road from 1968. Måsvägen and Doppingvägen east of the main road are streets from 1985; Doppingvägen includes the short unnamed piece that joins it to the main road.
+
+## Method, deferred and validation
+
+The method is unchanged: contact sheets and area crops (`lotsby-*`) in `pass5/`, `pass5/prepare.py` against the snapshot `pass5/before.json.gz`, and `scripts/mariehamn_street_pass5.py` with the shared validator (marker `mariehamnStreetPass5`). Deferred items are in the review file.
+
+`pass5/audit.py` confirms that the baseline equals the snapshot. The pass adds 26 objects (36,189 → 36,215), 221 geometries (46,839 → 47,060), all with the pass's prefix, and one source. Nothing existing changes.
+
+`tests/mariehamn-street-pass5.test.cjs` checks:
+
+- totals, including the 0 m junction;
+- starts and stable geometry;
+- single ownership against all earlier passes;
+- connection to roads drawn in the first edition;
+- the Stenliden anchoring;
+- the gap-piece dating rules.
+
+`tests/test_mariehamn_street_pass5.py` checks the compiler's rejections.
+
+**Publication.** Deployed 2026-11-12 as Cloudflare version `04f931de-8670-4551-b2e2-ab331cb34d07`. The release was prepared from the live version (`e9000b11…`) plus only this pass: the catalogue, `assets/mariehamn-street-pass5.json`, the loader card in `index.html`, and cache stamps in `temporal-objects.js` and `object.html`. Other unpublished workspace changes were left out. All 143 relevant JavaScript tests passed against the release tree, and all 288 live files were checked byte for byte against the release; see `pass5/deployment.json`.
